Compile the keymap in-process, through memfds (Linux).

RunXkbComp() forks and calls the built-in unpin_xkbcomp_main() instead of
running an external xkbcomp: the child keeps the binary and its embedded
xkeyboard-config tree, and a fresh address space per compile sidesteps
xkbcomp's non-reentrant globals. The spec and the compiled .xkm go through
two memfds (stdin and stdout of the child) instead of files in /tmp, and
XkbDDXOpenConfigFile() takes the .xkm fd RunXkbComp() hands it. fmemopen()
won't do: its buffer is not shared across fork().

Applied in postBuild, after unix/xserver21.patch, on the xorg-server tree
the build unpacks.

